faqs:
- q: Who does elderly removals in Northampton?
  a: Chayce Properties, based on Kingsthorpe Road in Northampton, specialises in elderly removals and downsizing across Northampton and Northamptonshire. One coordinator manages sorting, packing, fully insured removals, estate agent and solicitor liaison and settling in. Packages start at {bronze}, and a {discovery} Discovery Consultation gives you a plan and budget first. Call <a href="tel:+447708925432">07708 925432</a>.
- q: How much do removals in Northampton cost?
  a: Packages start at {bronze} for packing and removals, with full-service moves from {silver}. A Discovery Consultation costs {discovery} and gives you a personalised plan, timeline and budget before you commit to anything.
- q: Do you do house removals in Northampton for anyone?
  a: Yes. Our service is designed with older people in mind, but anyone who wants a fully managed house move in Northampton is welcome.
- q: Do you offer downsizing help for older people in Northampton?
  a: Yes. We help older people sort, pack, move and settle when downsizing, whether you are moving within the town, elsewhere in Northamptonshire or to another part of the UK.
- q: Which areas around Northampton do you cover?
  a: We work across Northamptonshire and the surrounding East Midlands, including <a href="/elderly-removals-kettering/">Kettering</a>, <a href="/elderly-removals-wellingborough/">Wellingborough</a>, <a href="/elderly-removals-daventry/">Daventry</a>, <a href="/elderly-removals-towcester/">Towcester</a>, <a href="/elderly-removals-brixworth/">Brixworth</a>, <a href="/elderly-removals-brackley/">Brackley</a>, <a href="/elderly-removals-desborough/">Desborough</a>, <a href="/elderly-removals-olney/">Olney</a>, <a href="/elderly-removals-rugby/">Rugby</a>, <a href="/elderly-removals-market-harborough/">Market Harborough</a>, <a href="/elderly-removals-milton-keynes/">Milton Keynes</a> and <a href="/elderly-removals-bedford/">Bedford</a>, as well as the rest of the UK.
- q: Can I visit your Northampton office?
  a: Yes. Our office is at Unit F2B Barratt House, Kingsthorpe Road, Northampton NN2 6EZ, open Monday to Friday 09:00 to 17:30. Please call <a href="tel:+447708925432">07708 925432</a> first so we can make sure a coordinator is available.
- q: Can you help with a care home move in Northampton?
  a: 'Yes, with the practical side: choosing what comes, packing, the removal and setting up the room. See <a href="/care-home-removals/">care home removals</a>.'
- q: Is the removal insured?
  a: Yes. Every Chayce removal is fully insured against loss or damage in transit, and the cover is set out in your service agreement before the move begins.
- q: Is Northampton in West Northamptonshire Council or North Northamptonshire Council?
  a: Northampton is in the West Northamptonshire Council area, along with Daventry, Brackley and Towcester. Kettering, Corby and Wellingborough are in the North Northamptonshire Council area. Our <a href="/blog/moving-in-northamptonshire-councils-council-tax/">guide to moving in Northamptonshire</a> explains which council to tell about your move.
- q: How do I tell the council I am moving within Northampton?
  a: 'West Northamptonshire Council lets you tell it that you have moved in, moved out or moved from one address to another within its area, through its <a href="https://www.westnorthants.gov.uk/council-tax/change-address" rel="noopener">Council Tax change of address page</a>.'
